# Document Processing System Architecture

## Core Components

The document processing system is organized in [src/app/components/document-processing/](mdc:src/app/components/document-processing/) with the following key components:

### Main Interface
- **DocumentAnalysisInterface.tsx** - Main unified interface for document analysis
- **LegacyDocumentProcessor.tsx** - Legacy Grok processing interface (deprecated)

### Query Management
- **QueryHistoryList.tsx** - List component for displaying query history
- **QueryHistoryDashboard.tsx** - Main dashboard page for query history
- **RecentQueriesWidget.tsx** - Widget showing recent queries
- **QueryAnalyticsDashboard.tsx** - Dashboard with analytics and statistics
- **QueryDetailsModal.tsx** - Modal for displaying detailed query information

### Processing Components
- **ProcessingStatusIndicators.tsx** - Components for showing processing status and progress

## File Naming Conventions

All files are named based on their functionality:
- Interface components: `[Feature]Interface.tsx`
- List components: `[Feature]List.tsx`
- Dashboard components: `[Feature]Dashboard.tsx`
- Widget components: `[Feature]Widget.tsx`
- Modal components: `[Feature]Modal.tsx`
- Status components: `[Feature]StatusIndicators.tsx`

## Component Hierarchy

```
DocumentAnalysisInterface (Main)
├── Search Tab
├── Files Tab (OneDrive integration)
├── History Tab
└── Sidebar
    ├── Quick Tools
    ├── Recent Queries
    └── Quick Prompts
```

## Integration Points

- **OneDrive Integration**: Files tab uses OneDriveInterface component
- **Query History**: Uses useQueryHistory hook for data management
- **Processing**: Uses useDocumentProcessing hook for real-time processing
- **Authentication**: Integrated with NextAuth session management